@ 6.1.1 - Proto-Omotic to North Omotic
# citation: Mecislau, from Ehret, Christopher (1995), Reconstructing Proto-Afroasiatic (Proto-Afrasian): Vowels, Tone, Consonants, and Vocabulary (Voices from Asia)
	u o > i e
	e > i / #N_C
	e > i / #l_{P,C:[+voice]}
	e > i / #b_
	e > i / p_r
	e > i / #{s,ʃ,t͡sʼ}_{kʷ,ʔ}
	e o > i u / #C_P
	e o > i u / #(ʔ)_C
	e o > i u / #{kʼ,x}_{tʼ,t͡sʼ}
	e o > i u / #(ʔ)_C$
	e o > i u / #P_{t͡sʼ,t͡ʃʼ}
	a > o / #{z,d͡ʒ}_P
	{ e, e:[+long] } > { i, i:[+long] } / #C:[+strident]_{d,n,r}
	Cw > C
	V:[+long] > V / #[+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo, -voice]_C
	u > u:[+long] / #S:[+voice]_P:[-voice]
	V:[+long] > V / #C_C$
	N > ∅ / V_{C:[+strident],p}